# INTRODUCTION

1. First go the splunk official website and sign in afree account.

2. Choose Linux and download the .deb package. Alternatively, 

   grab the wget link from their page to download it directly in your terminal:

command :

    wget -O splunk-installer.deb "YOUR_SPLUNK_DOWNLOAD_LINK"

3. Open your terminal and navigate to your download folder:

Command :
   cd ~/Downloads

4. Install the package using the Debian package manager:

Command :
   sudo dpkg -i splunk-*.deb

5. Navigate to the Splunk executable folder and start the service:

Command :
   cd /opt/splunk/bin
   sudo ./splunk start --accept-license

6. Access the Splunk Web UI by opening your browser and entering 
   http://localhost:8000 
   (Instead of localhost if you open the splunk in your host machine browser 
    you type ip of kali linux:8000)



